Q: jQuery menu animation behaving weird A: <p>Before your <code>slideUp</code> and <code>slideDown</code> use the jQuery <code>stop()</code> method (<a href="http://api.jquery.com/stop/" rel="nofollow"><strong>docs</strong></a>) to clear the animation queue.  For example from your code:</p>

<pre><code>jQuery('ul', this).stop(true, true).slideDown('fast');
</code></pre>

Q: Is there a &quot;right&quot; way to have NSTextFieldCell draw vertically centered text? A: <p>I found that I simply had to overload NSCells <code>-drawingRectForBounds:</code></p>
<p>and implement it like so</p>
<pre><code>- (NSRect)drawingRectForBounds:(NSRect)rect
{
    NSFont * font = self.font;
    return NSRectFromCGRect(CGRectMake(rect.origin.x, rect.origin.y + font.xHeight / 2, rect.size.width, rect.size.height)); // maybe the baseline is a better metric
}
</code></pre>
